Subject: nak: fix max_warps_per_sm for MR !37898 ABI

MR !37898 (nvk_cubin / DLSS) calls nak_max_warps_per_sm() with a
signature that expects the computation to live here rather than
forwarding to crate::ir::max_warps_per_sm.  Inline the formula directly.

Zero-context (-U0) so patch --fuzz tolerates any surrounding refactors.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/api.rs
@@ -2,1 +2,3 @@
-    crate::ir::max_warps_per_sm(num_gprs)
+    let total_regs: u32 = 65536;
+    let gprs = num_gprs.max(1).next_multiple_of(8);
+    crate::ir::prev_multiple_of((total_regs / 32) / gprs, 4)
